WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:05.921
It's been five days since
I debuted as a professional hero.

00:00:06.421 --> 00:00:08.511
There haven't been any serious incidents so far.

00:00:09.551 --> 00:00:13.931
However, Genos is now living with me for some reason.

00:00:14.931 --> 00:00:16.931
What are you writing over there?

00:00:16.931 --> 00:00:20.231
I'm recording the details of your lessons and training regimen.

00:00:20.641 --> 00:00:23.191
Crap. He's raising the bar again…

00:00:23.651 --> 00:00:26.651
I can't think of a single thing I can teach the guy.

00:00:26.651 --> 00:00:29.781
I feel like I'm scamming him or something.

00:00:29.781 --> 00:00:30.571
Come on, think.

00:00:30.571 --> 00:00:34.281
At least make up some techniques
or a spiritual theory.

00:00:34.281 --> 00:00:36.201
Argh, strength training's all I've got!

00:00:36.201 --> 00:00:37.741
But I know that won't satisfy Genos!

00:00:37.741 --> 00:00:38.911
Plus, he's a cyborg!

00:00:38.911 --> 00:00:39.291
By the way,

00:00:40.121 --> 00:00:45.381
at the seminar, they said C-class heroes
who are inactive for a week

00:00:45.381 --> 00:00:48.091
are removed from the Hero Registry.

00:00:48.091 --> 00:00:49.251
Aren't you cutting it close?

00:00:50.131 --> 00:00:51.921
They said that?!

00:00:51.921 --> 00:00:52.341
Yes.

00:00:52.341 --> 00:00:55.591
But I was watching TV and
there wasn't anything going on.

00:00:55.591 --> 00:00:59.181
The news only reports major incidents,

00:00:59.181 --> 00:01:02.311
like natural disasters, terrorism, and dangerous monsters.

00:01:02.731 --> 00:01:06.561
You always fight the most powerful enemies,
so this is probably new to you,

00:01:07.021 --> 00:01:09.821
but C-class heroes primarily
take care of purse snatchers,

00:01:09.821 --> 00:01:12.241
robberies, and random attacks.

00:01:12.241 --> 00:01:13.821
With Class C so full of heroes,

00:01:13.821 --> 00:01:16.661
they must actively look for cases to resolve in order to stay afloat.

00:01:16.661 --> 00:01:19.081
I hear many of them get discouraged
and change careers.

00:01:19.411 --> 00:01:24.331
Like a salesman doing cold calls,
nothing will come your way without legwork.

00:01:24.661 --> 00:01:26.581
This is no time to be reading manga!

00:01:27.171 --> 00:01:28.081
So we're going?

00:01:28.081 --> 00:01:29.211
You stay here!

00:01:29.211 --> 00:01:33.341
If I'm with an S-class hero,
a C-class like me won't get any credit!

00:01:33.341 --> 00:01:34.921
But as your apprentice—

00:01:36.341 --> 00:01:38.761
Genos, from the beginning,

00:01:38.761 --> 00:01:42.721
my intense desire to be a hero was
what drove me to strength training.

00:01:42.721 --> 00:01:44.311
That's how I made it this far.

00:01:44.981 --> 00:01:50.481
Perhaps things will change for you too
if you set higher goals for yourself as a hero.

00:01:51.521 --> 00:01:52.981
Frankly speaking, you're a cyborg,

00:01:53.481 --> 00:01:55.491
so there's no point in training your body.

00:01:55.491 --> 00:01:58.621
Instead, a change in mindset
may lead you to greater strength.

00:02:00.491 --> 00:02:03.661
Damn, I'm just making all this crap up…

00:02:05.041 --> 00:02:07.001
So… in other words,

00:02:07.001 --> 00:02:10.461
it's not about having raw power or technique.

00:02:07.001 --> 00:02:13.251
H

00:02:07.001 --> 00:02:13.251
O

00:02:07.001 --> 00:02:13.251
W

00:02:07.001 --> 00:02:13.251
I

00:02:07.001 --> 00:02:13.251
D

00:02:07.001 --> 00:02:13.251
E

00:02:07.001 --> 00:02:13.251
V

00:02:07.001 --> 00:02:13.251
L

00:02:07.001 --> 00:02:13.251
P

00:02:07.001 --> 00:02:13.251
N

00:02:07.001 --> 00:02:13.251
M

00:02:07.001 --> 00:02:13.251
T

00:02:07.001 --> 00:02:13.251
A

00:02:07.001 --> 00:02:13.251
B

00:02:07.001 --> 00:02:13.251
Y

00:02:07.001 --> 00:02:13.251
S-CLASS

00:02:07.001 --> 00:02:13.251
R

00:02:07.001 --> 00:02:13.251
K

00:02:07.001 --> 00:02:13.251
G

00:02:10.461 --> 00:02:12.671
It's about training your mind.

00:02:12.671 --> 00:02:16.341
To do that, you must first fight your way through the pro hero industry.

00:02:16.341 --> 00:02:19.891
Aim to break into the top ten of Class S.

00:02:19.891 --> 00:02:22.311
That's a good place to start.

00:02:24.601 --> 00:02:25.561
I understand.

00:02:26.021 --> 00:02:27.231
I will try!

00:02:27.231 --> 00:02:29.851
He bought it, sweet!

00:02:36.191 --> 00:02:40.321
After that, I sped around town,
frantically looking for bad guys.

00:02:41.161 --> 00:02:41.821
I ran,

00:02:42.491 --> 00:02:43.161
and ran,

00:02:43.701 --> 00:02:44.831
and ran.

00:02:45.411 --> 00:02:45.911
But!

00:02:47.251 --> 00:02:49.041
There was no sign of trouble anywhere!

00:02:50.421 --> 00:02:52.041
I give up.

00:02:53.631 --> 00:02:55.511
Just one more day left.

00:02:59.221 --> 00:03:00.761
Guess I'll head home.

00:03:04.311 --> 00:03:07.431
I'll leave tomorrow's problems to tomorrow's me.

00:03:18.321 --> 00:03:22.071
ONE PUNCH

00:03:25.781 --> 00:03:27.531
THREE, TWO, ONE, KILL SHOT

00:03:27.531 --> 00:03:31.291
JOIN THE FIGHT, CERTAIN VICTORY, THE STRONGEST EVER

00:03:27.531 --> 00:03:31.291
SANJOU, HISSHOU, SHIJOU SAIKYOU

00:03:31.291 --> 00:03:33.291
WHAT WAS THAT? FRUSTRATION

00:03:31.291 --> 00:03:33.291
NAN DATTEN DA? FRUSTRATION

00:03:33.291 --> 00:03:34.791
THERE'S NO STOPPING ME

00:03:33.291 --> 00:03:34.791
ORE WA TOMARANAI

00:03:34.791 --> 00:03:38.921
ONE PUNCH, IT'S OVER, VICTORY AFTER VICTORY

00:03:34.791 --> 00:03:38.921
ONE PUNCH, KANRYOU, RENSENRENSHOU

00:03:38.921 --> 00:03:42.551
I WIN, I ALWAYS WIN, OVERWHELMINGLY

00:03:38.921 --> 00:03:42.551
ORE WA KATSU, TSUNE NI KATSU, ASSHOU

00:03:42.551 --> 00:03:46.391
POWER, GET POWER

00:03:46.391 --> 00:03:49.351
RIGHT TO THE VERY LIMIT

00:03:46.391 --> 00:03:49.351
GIRIGIRI GENKAI MADE

00:03:49.351 --> 00:03:50.561
HERO

00:03:50.561 --> 00:03:53.731
PEOPLE SHOWER ME WITH PRAISE

00:03:50.561 --> 00:03:53.731
ORE O TATAERU KOE YA

00:03:53.731 --> 00:03:56.771
BUT I DON'T DO THIS FOR THE FAME

00:03:53.731 --> 00:03:56.771
KASSAI NANTE HOSHIKU WA NAI SA

00:03:56.771 --> 00:03:58.021
HERO

00:03:58.021 --> 00:04:02.781
SO I JUST FIGHT EVIL IN SECRET

00:03:58.021 --> 00:04:02.781
DAKARA HITOSHIREZU AKU TO TATAKAU

00:04:02.781 --> 00:04:04.241
(NOBODY KNOWS WHO HE IS)

00:04:04.241 --> 00:04:08.411
COUNTLESS ENEMIES FILL THE SKY

00:04:04.241 --> 00:04:08.411
SORA OOI OSHIYOSERU TEKI

00:04:08.411 --> 00:04:11.491
BUT I WON'T TURN MY BACK AND FLEE

00:04:08.411 --> 00:04:11.491
ORE WA SE WO MUKE WA SHINAI

00:04:11.491 --> 00:04:12.831
HERO

00:04:12.831 --> 00:04:17.831
I'VE MADE UP MY MIND AND I WON'T GIVE IN

00:04:12.831 --> 00:04:17.831
NARABA YURUGINAKI KAKUGO SHITA TAME

00:04:17.831 --> 00:04:25.051
A FIGHTING HERO

00:04:17.831 --> 00:04:25.051
TATAKAU HERO

00:04:25.051 --> 00:04:31.601
A SOLITARY HERO

00:04:25.051 --> 00:04:31.601
KODOKU NA HERO

00:04:31.601 --> 00:04:36.601
I WANNA BE THE STRONGEST HERO

00:04:31.601 --> 00:04:36.601
I WANNA BE A SAIKYOU HERO

00:04:39.021 --> 00:04:41.531
THE FOLLOWING DAY

00:04:44.071 --> 00:04:46.031
It's all quiet today too!

00:04:46.031 --> 00:04:48.781
There's nothing to do!

00:04:49.081 --> 00:04:51.251
I'm gonna lose my registration!

00:04:55.501 --> 00:04:58.051
Hey! You're that guy…

00:04:58.631 --> 00:04:59.761
What was it again?

00:05:01.171 --> 00:05:02.801
"Seed-on-the-Ground"?

00:05:02.801 --> 00:05:04.721
No wait, "Lost-and-Found"?

00:05:04.721 --> 00:05:06.471
Ah, Jack-o'-Lantern Panic!

00:05:06.471 --> 00:05:08.471
It's Speed-o'-Sound Sonic.

00:05:09.141 --> 00:05:11.731
I've finally found you, Saitama.

00:05:12.101 --> 00:05:13.641
Today is the day we—

00:05:13.641 --> 00:05:16.191
Sorry, I'm busy. See you 'round.

00:05:17.571 --> 00:05:18.321
Huh?

00:05:19.151 --> 00:05:20.651
You think…

00:05:21.491 --> 00:05:23.441
you can run from me?!

00:05:26.871 --> 00:05:27.741
What the—?

00:05:27.741 --> 00:05:28.951
I didn't see what happened.

00:05:29.991 --> 00:05:33.121
His face should have been
sliced open, but the blade…

00:05:33.711 --> 00:05:37.081
I told you, I'm busy.

00:05:38.291 --> 00:05:40.921
And I'm pissed off, so anyone in my way…

00:05:43.381 --> 00:05:44.431
gets punched.

00:05:46.551 --> 00:05:47.181
That's him!

00:05:47.761 --> 00:05:48.931
He's very dangerous.

00:05:49.261 --> 00:05:51.181
Please stop him.

00:05:51.181 --> 00:05:52.481
It's you, eh?!

00:05:52.481 --> 00:05:57.771
Well, your hero, Tank-Top Tiger, is here now!

00:05:59.071 --> 00:06:00.531
Hero?

00:06:01.651 --> 00:06:04.531
Sonic, they think you're some sort of criminal.

00:06:05.031 --> 00:06:07.621
Maybe getting tossed in a cell
will cool off your hot—

00:06:08.491 --> 00:06:10.281
She means you, cueball.

00:06:11.331 --> 00:06:12.541
Huh?

00:06:12.541 --> 00:06:17.671
He's been running around town with this scary look on his face since yesterday!

00:06:17.671 --> 00:06:19.291
But I'm a hero too!

00:06:19.291 --> 00:06:22.341
I've never heard of a hero like you.

00:06:22.341 --> 00:06:24.301
So what? I just started!

00:06:24.301 --> 00:06:25.051
In any case,

00:06:25.421 --> 00:06:28.091
you're causing problems for everyone.

00:06:28.091 --> 00:06:31.811
If you really are a hero,
then don't go around frightening people.

00:06:31.811 --> 00:06:34.481
You're hurting all our reputations.

00:06:34.481 --> 00:06:36.521
Hey isn't that Tank-Top Tiger?

00:06:36.891 --> 00:06:39.021
Oh yeah, it is Tank-Top Tiger.

00:06:39.021 --> 00:06:39.521
No way!

00:06:39.861 --> 00:06:41.691
Awesome, he's the real deal!

00:06:45.491 --> 00:06:49.871
Even C-class heroes get recognized
if they're in the top 10.

00:06:51.031 --> 00:06:53.121
So, how 'bout it, new guy?

00:06:53.121 --> 00:06:57.041
Wanna go a little wild here and make me look good?

00:06:57.041 --> 00:06:58.621
Exploding Shuriken.

00:06:59.081 --> 00:07:01.631
What the—?!

00:07:00.711 --> 00:07:02.461
EXPLODING SHURIKEN

00:07:05.881 --> 00:07:06.721
Tank-Top Tiger?!

00:07:07.341 --> 00:07:09.011
Is this really happening?

00:07:09.011 --> 00:07:11.681
What are you doing, Sonic?

00:07:11.681 --> 00:07:15.391
He was interfering, so I put him to sleep.

00:07:15.391 --> 00:07:16.811
Hey, call a hero!

00:07:16.811 --> 00:07:17.731
A hero!

00:07:17.731 --> 00:07:19.441
Run!

00:07:20.271 --> 00:07:21.361
Saitama…

00:07:21.901 --> 00:07:26.191
So you too have become one of
these worthless "heroes"?

00:07:27.321 --> 00:07:29.451
In that case, all I have to do is

00:07:29.451 --> 00:07:33.741
create a situation where you have no choice
but to fight me, Saitama the Hero!

00:07:35.291 --> 00:07:36.581
Hail of Carnage!

00:07:42.711 --> 00:07:43.541
Huh?

00:07:47.381 --> 00:07:48.591
Hey! Cut it out!

00:07:48.591 --> 00:07:51.301
Saitama, come stop me!

00:07:51.841 --> 00:07:53.181
Aren't you a hero?!

00:07:53.181 --> 00:07:54.971
I'm gonna kill 'em all!

00:08:01.481 --> 00:08:02.521
Dammit.

00:08:03.021 --> 00:08:05.151
Can't everyone just let me do my job?

00:08:05.781 --> 00:08:08.191
I don't have time for this!

00:08:09.451 --> 00:08:11.781
I gotta find a bad guy to take down.

00:08:16.041 --> 00:08:17.081
A bad guy?

00:08:18.331 --> 00:08:20.581
If you're not coming, I'll come to you!

00:08:20.921 --> 00:08:21.831
I'm right here.

00:08:31.511 --> 00:08:33.971
I wonder if this'll count as work?

00:08:35.931 --> 00:08:39.641
The man apprehended in City Z by the C-class hero

00:08:39.641 --> 00:08:43.901
is suspected of being involved in several heinous crimes, including assassination.

00:08:45.771 --> 00:08:47.191
City Z…

00:08:49.651 --> 00:08:51.991
What's the status of the investigation I requested?

00:08:52.281 --> 00:08:54.031
The one for the ghost town?

00:08:54.031 --> 00:08:54.661
Yes.

00:08:54.661 --> 00:08:55.991
Let's see…

00:08:57.241 --> 00:08:59.751
We've submitted an official request.

00:09:01.291 --> 00:09:04.581
Well now, doesn't that sound interesting?

00:09:04.581 --> 00:09:05.961
Want me to go?

00:09:05.961 --> 00:09:07.001
T-Tatsumaki?

00:09:07.671 --> 00:09:08.961
Where'd you come from?

00:09:08.961 --> 00:09:11.051
Why? Aren't I allowed in here?

00:09:11.051 --> 00:09:11.921
Of course.

00:09:11.921 --> 00:09:15.141
But the City Z investigation is just a formality.

00:09:15.141 --> 00:09:16.011
What?

00:09:17.301 --> 00:09:19.521
You think I'm not good enough?

00:09:23.271 --> 00:09:24.021
Not at all.

00:09:24.481 --> 00:09:28.401
The Association decided that
this didn't concern Class S.

00:09:28.401 --> 00:09:30.531
Yes, precisely.

00:09:35.161 --> 00:09:38.621
You'd better tell me if you find
anything that looks like it can fight.

00:09:42.291 --> 00:09:44.621
It'd be so much faster if I just went myself.

00:09:45.541 --> 00:09:46.961
You're such an idiot.

00:10:14.361 --> 00:10:18.071
CITY A

00:10:14.361 --> 00:10:18.071
HERO ASSOCIATION HQ

00:10:16.321 --> 00:10:19.371
Reports have come in from
each location under investigation.

00:10:22.031 --> 00:10:25.081
First is Watchdog Man, Class S,
investigating City Q.

00:10:25.081 --> 00:10:26.161
"Nothing unusual."

00:10:26.161 --> 00:10:27.411
Nothing unusual?

00:10:27.411 --> 00:10:28.121
That's right.

00:10:28.121 --> 00:10:29.751
That's hard to believe.

00:10:29.751 --> 00:10:36.011
We all know City Q is a hot spot with more
casualties and monsters than any other area.

00:10:36.011 --> 00:10:42.891
Knowing him, I'm sure he's implying that he'll
be able to take care of anything that happens.

00:10:43.431 --> 00:10:46.481
Though he has focused his efforts on City Q,

00:10:46.481 --> 00:10:49.771
his monster elimination track record is top-notch.

00:10:49.771 --> 00:10:52.231
S-class heroes don't pay much attention to detail.

00:10:52.231 --> 00:10:54.651
They're not cut out for writing reports.

00:10:54.651 --> 00:10:56.991
Next, City W.

00:10:56.991 --> 00:10:58.861
A-class hero Heavy Kong reports:

00:10:58.861 --> 00:10:59.661
"Nothing unusual."

00:11:00.571 --> 00:11:04.031
For City H, reports from Mushroom, Class B, and Horsebone, Class C:

00:11:04.031 --> 00:11:04.661
"Nothing unusual."

00:11:05.241 --> 00:11:08.081
City D, Lightning Genji, Class A, reports:

00:11:08.081 --> 00:11:13.591
"Aside from slow restoration after the devastation caused by the gigantic creature, nothing unusual."

00:11:13.591 --> 00:11:17.011
Cities B and D both sustained extensive damage.

00:11:17.011 --> 00:11:19.551
The Association took a lot of heat for that.

00:11:19.551 --> 00:11:22.181
To prevent similar disasters in the future,

00:11:22.181 --> 00:11:26.311
we must detect any covert activity
that could threaten the community.

00:11:26.811 --> 00:11:30.641
Well, this investigation was
requested for that express purpose.

00:11:30.641 --> 00:11:33.561
But early detection of monsters is proving difficult.

00:11:34.441 --> 00:11:37.571
From City F, Snakebite Snek, Class A:

00:11:38.241 --> 00:11:44.071
"Hammerhead, former leader of the Paradiser terrorist group, has been spotted in a suit and tie.

00:11:44.071 --> 00:11:45.701
Further investigation is being conducted."

00:11:46.081 --> 00:11:47.291
No other reports.

00:11:47.291 --> 00:11:48.701
What of City Z?

00:11:49.211 --> 00:11:54.171
I hear rumblings of a potential disaster
brewing in the abandoned district there.

00:11:54.171 --> 00:11:56.211
No reports available.

00:11:56.631 --> 00:12:03.341
However, two highly capable A-class heroes have been sent to the area to investigate.

00:12:05.391 --> 00:12:07.221
Here we are in City Z.

00:12:08.471 --> 00:12:11.731
CLASS A, RANK 33
SPRING MUSTACHIO

00:12:08.851 --> 00:12:11.731
Shall we begin our little inquiry?

00:12:11.931 --> 00:12:15.561
CLASS A, RANK 29
GOLDEN BALL

00:12:12.391 --> 00:12:15.191
Yeah, let's get on with it.

00:12:20.651 --> 00:12:23.071
City Z is quite expansive,

00:12:23.071 --> 00:12:27.741
but further ahead lies the uninhabited district we were told about.

00:12:27.741 --> 00:12:32.871
Compared with other areas, City Z has an
abnormally high rate of monster-related incidents.

00:12:28.621 --> 00:12:32.871
BEWARE OF
MONSTERS!!

00:12:33.831 --> 00:12:37.501
The frequency has been gradually increasing over the past decade,

00:12:37.501 --> 00:12:40.631
while the last few years have seen more and more
highly advanced monsters appearing.

00:12:41.341 --> 00:12:44.761
The residents have all fled for the city center.

00:12:44.761 --> 00:12:46.181
I know all that.

00:12:46.181 --> 00:12:51.061
The place is a real ghost town,
just with utilities still working, yeah?

00:12:51.061 --> 00:12:53.311
On the lookout for a cheap house?

00:12:53.311 --> 00:12:54.141
Come off it.

00:12:55.021 --> 00:12:57.861
People say something real nasty's living 'round here.

00:12:57.861 --> 00:12:59.941
Even you must've heard 'bout it.

00:12:59.941 --> 00:13:01.401
But of course.

00:13:01.401 --> 00:13:05.661
I assume that's why we were
assigned this investigation.

00:13:06.201 --> 00:13:10.701
Once we hit the abandoned district, we better be ready to fight.

00:13:10.701 --> 00:13:14.621
Indeed, we mustn't let our guard down.

00:13:16.001 --> 00:13:19.421
But why here? Why the increase in monsters?

00:13:19.421 --> 00:13:21.591
That's the mystery.

00:13:21.591 --> 00:13:25.511
Many theories have been proposed,
but my own is this:

00:13:25.511 --> 00:13:29.101
A colony of monsters here is naturally breeding.

00:13:29.101 --> 00:13:32.061
Or perhaps a queen exists,
spawning more of her kind.

00:13:35.441 --> 00:13:38.861
Of course, I have no proof yet,

00:13:38.861 --> 00:13:41.571
but there is something to this ghost town.

00:13:42.111 --> 00:13:44.031
Or rather, something in it.

00:13:44.651 --> 00:13:46.911
There's no denying that.

00:13:48.571 --> 00:13:50.531
The proximity alarm?

00:13:50.831 --> 00:13:52.751
If we can hunt down this monster,

00:13:52.751 --> 00:13:55.371
we'll go straight to the top of the rankings.

00:13:55.371 --> 00:13:56.711
That's true.

00:13:56.711 --> 00:13:59.131
We can't let Amai Mask remain first for—

00:13:59.881 --> 00:14:00.751
Behind us?!

00:14:01.051 --> 00:14:02.461
Was that a monster?

00:14:02.461 --> 00:14:04.091
No way to be sure.

00:14:04.421 --> 00:14:07.971
But it's hard to imagine a human still living in these conditions.

00:14:08.761 --> 00:14:10.141
Let's pursue it!

00:14:13.521 --> 00:14:15.521
Seems they aren't after us.

00:14:18.151 --> 00:14:20.401
Could this be the place I heard about?

00:14:20.861 --> 00:14:23.571
Sure don't seem like it…

00:14:23.571 --> 00:14:26.651
Aw man, I came all this way.

00:14:26.651 --> 00:14:27.911
Isn't anyone around?

00:14:30.951 --> 00:14:32.201
A monster.

00:14:32.201 --> 00:14:33.491
It popped up out of nowhere.

00:14:34.201 --> 00:14:36.541
Golden Ball, are you ready?

00:14:36.541 --> 00:14:37.661
Hell yeah!

00:14:37.661 --> 00:14:39.421
Victory to the swift!

00:14:39.711 --> 00:14:40.921
Hey, people!

00:14:41.341 --> 00:14:45.961
My golden shape-memory bullets can blast through a 20mm steel plate!

00:14:46.511 --> 00:14:47.761
Eat this!

00:14:56.271 --> 00:14:57.851
They swatted it away like a fly!

00:15:10.911 --> 00:15:11.661
Golden!

00:15:42.601 --> 00:15:43.981
Wow!

00:15:54.321 --> 00:15:55.241
Tomboy…

00:15:57.371 --> 00:15:58.121
Thrust!

00:16:01.371 --> 00:16:04.081
I-It slipped past my Tomboy?!

00:16:10.841 --> 00:16:12.221
Not bad.

00:16:12.841 --> 00:16:14.301
Those tentacles…

00:16:14.301 --> 00:16:16.471
They must be as tough as steel.

00:16:16.971 --> 00:16:21.731
A monster that can use its infinite tentacles like steel whips…

00:16:22.391 --> 00:16:23.521
Such power!

00:16:27.941 --> 00:16:30.401
I must call in reinforcements from the Association.

00:16:31.451 --> 00:16:36.331
May I ask if you were born in this neighborhood?

00:16:37.701 --> 00:16:39.701
Nah, I'm from out of town.

00:16:40.121 --> 00:16:44.791
I heard a bunch of crazy strong monsters were all getting together here.

00:16:44.791 --> 00:16:49.001
Looks like it was just a rumor though.

00:16:49.001 --> 00:16:50.341
But now,

00:16:52.221 --> 00:16:57.551
I feel like it'd be kinda fun to stick around
and make the rumor true.

00:16:57.931 --> 00:16:59.601
The Ghost Town Monster…

00:17:00.271 --> 00:17:02.681
It's got a nice ring to it!

00:17:03.641 --> 00:17:07.691
We have a backup request from the heroes dispatched to City Z.

00:17:07.691 --> 00:17:10.981
Class A rank 29, Golden Ball, has been knocked out.

00:17:10.981 --> 00:17:13.951
Class A rank 33, Spring Mustachio, is in trouble.

00:17:13.951 --> 00:17:15.611
They're in the abandoned city.

00:17:15.611 --> 00:17:18.581
Call in all nearby heroes for immediate assistance!

00:17:18.581 --> 00:17:19.581
Class A and above!

00:17:20.451 --> 00:17:22.661
You see the monster alert for City Z?

00:17:22.661 --> 00:17:25.291
The threat level seems to be Tiger, maybe higher.

00:17:25.671 --> 00:17:27.421
Is it the ghost town monster?

00:17:27.421 --> 00:17:29.841
They're not sure yet.

00:17:29.841 --> 00:17:30.751
I'll go.

00:17:32.261 --> 00:17:34.881
I want to catch the tiger by the tail.

00:17:47.101 --> 00:17:48.151
Now I get it…

00:17:48.771 --> 00:17:51.651
If it meant running into monsters like this all the time,

00:17:52.151 --> 00:17:56.071
I wouldn't want to live here either.

00:17:59.121 --> 00:18:00.581
Man, how boring.

00:18:00.581 --> 00:18:02.161
This is so boring!

00:18:02.161 --> 00:18:05.911
I finally kick a hero's butt and
I don't get even a single scream.

00:18:06.541 --> 00:18:10.251
Now that I think about it,
even if I start living here,

00:18:10.251 --> 00:18:12.591
I'll never be famous if no one's around.

00:18:13.421 --> 00:18:17.721
Guess I'll keep going.
Gotta find where they live.

00:18:19.391 --> 00:18:20.851
Someone's here.

00:18:21.261 --> 00:18:23.021
Another hero?

00:18:24.021 --> 00:18:25.101
Or a regular guy?

00:18:25.811 --> 00:18:28.901
I thought all the humans cleared out.

00:18:28.901 --> 00:18:32.691
If so many monsters really live here,
there's no way he could stick around.

00:18:34.741 --> 00:18:38.611
I guess that means it was just a rumor.

00:18:38.611 --> 00:18:39.701
Shoot…

00:18:41.071 --> 00:18:43.201
I forgot to buy kelp soup stock.

00:18:47.461 --> 00:18:51.131
Master, I saw a lot of kelp right outside the door.

00:18:51.131 --> 00:18:53.711
Oh yeah, I just…

00:18:54.881 --> 00:18:58.761
just happened… to get it for cheap.

00:19:02.261 --> 00:19:07.061
People do say that kelp is good for hair growth,
but since there is no real scientific proof,

00:19:07.061 --> 00:19:09.141
its real effects are unconfirmed.

00:19:09.811 --> 00:19:12.441
I did some research, so I am sure, Master.

00:19:13.151 --> 00:19:15.111
For example, according to this site—

00:19:15.111 --> 00:19:16.651
No one said anything about hair!

00:19:17.491 --> 00:19:19.151
City Z Investigative Report.

00:19:19.571 --> 00:19:23.161
"Nothing noteworthy about the downtown or residential areas.

00:19:23.741 --> 00:19:28.501
During our investigation, we encountered a ferocious monster in the abandoned district,

00:19:28.501 --> 00:19:30.371
but were unable to exterminate it.

00:19:30.371 --> 00:19:31.961
We escaped death,

00:19:31.961 --> 00:19:37.051
but the monster we encountered disappeared and it is possible that it still roams the area.

00:19:37.051 --> 00:19:39.091
Also, according to this monster,

00:19:39.091 --> 00:19:43.931
there's a rumor that powerful monsters
already exist in the area."

00:19:44.761 --> 00:19:47.931
Sounds like it was pretty brutal.

00:19:48.391 --> 00:19:49.691
A monster?

00:19:49.691 --> 00:19:50.941
Y-Yes.

00:19:53.691 --> 00:19:55.441
I think I'll pass this time.

00:19:55.731 --> 00:19:58.821
See? I told you I should have gone!

00:19:58.821 --> 00:19:59.951
But…

00:20:00.361 --> 00:20:02.411
If you were faced with this,

00:20:02.411 --> 00:20:06.411
I'm sure even you would have had a tough time.

00:20:10.291 --> 00:20:13.831
I would have been fine, moron.

00:20:15.001 --> 00:20:17.381
The rumor has not been confirmed,

00:20:17.381 --> 00:20:22.301
but the reinforcements witnessed
evidence of some horrible monstrosity.

00:20:22.301 --> 00:20:24.891
Holy crap, what is this?

00:20:24.891 --> 00:20:27.561
What kind of monster could be so destructive?

00:20:27.561 --> 00:20:30.231
I'd hate to face off against this thing.

00:20:30.681 --> 00:20:32.731
Hey, what's this?

00:20:33.771 --> 00:20:37.191
Is it a part of the monster Spring Mustachio fought?

00:20:37.191 --> 00:20:40.191
There must've been a territorial dispute between monsters.

00:20:40.941 --> 00:20:44.241
Seems like there's definitely something here.

00:20:45.491 --> 00:20:49.751
We must continue our investigation and maintain vigilance over City Z.

00:20:52.161 --> 00:20:53.501
Hey, did you hear?

00:20:53.501 --> 00:20:55.961
There are monsters living in the City Z ghost town.

00:20:56.631 --> 00:21:01.171
Yeah, rumor has it the toughest ones are secretly plotting something.

00:21:01.171 --> 00:21:05.681
No, no. There's a rumor about an even more dangerous monster.

00:21:05.681 --> 00:21:06.851
What's that?

00:21:06.851 --> 00:21:08.101
You haven't heard?

00:21:08.101 --> 00:21:13.141
Apparently, the place has now become
terrifying for both humans and monsters.

00:21:13.561 --> 00:21:18.061
